<h2>
<font color="brown"> Frequently Asked Questions</font>
</h2>

<details>

<summary>
<b>What is investing?</b>
</summary>

Investing means putting money into assets with the goal of generating returns over time.

</details>

<br>

<details>

<summary>
<b>Is investing different from saving?</b>
</summary>

Yes. Saving generally focuses on keeping money safe and accessible, while investing involves taking some level of risk for potential growth.

</details>

<br>

<details>

<summary>
<b>Can beginners start investing?</b>
</summary>

Yes. Beginners can start by learning basic financial concepts and choosing investments that match their goals and risk tolerance.

</details>

<br>

<details>

<summary>
<b>Why is financial planning important?</b>
</summary>

Financial planning helps you manage income, expenses, savings and long-term financial goals.

</details>

